# Saas-Booking – Project Rules

You are working inside the **Saas-Booking** monorepo project.

Technology stack:
- Backend: Node.js, Express, TypeScript, MongoDB (Mongoose)
- Frontend: Angular 20 (Standalone APIs)
- Auth: JWT via HTTP-only cookies + optional Bearer token
- Architecture: Multi-tenant (businessId required on all requests)
- Repo type: Monorepo (apps/api, apps/frontend-web)

==================================================
CORE DOMAIN RULES
==================================================
1. Every backend request must be scoped under **businessId** from the authenticated user.
2. Never trust businessId coming directly from the client.
3. Always validate user role & permissions before executing business-sensitive operations.
4. Controllers must be thin; move logic into services.
5. Use async/await only (no promise chains).
6. Keep logic testable and side-effect free when possible.

==================================================
FRONTEND (ANGULAR) RULES
==================================================
1. Use Angular Standalone Components only.
2. Use strict lazy-loading by route.
3. Each domain is a vertical module under:
   src/app/modules/<domain>/
   with folders:
   - pages/
   - components/
   - services/
   - dto/
   - model/

4. Shared logic goes under:
   - src/app/core/ (api, auth, guards, layout)
   - src/app/shared/ (ui, services, pipes, directives, types)

5. Pages are route-level components only.
6. Components must NOT call HttpClient directly.
   All HTTP logic goes through services.

==================================================
CSS / SCSS CONVENTIONS (MANDATORY)
==================================================
- Use **kebab-case class names only**
- DO NOT use BEM syntax
- DO NOT use "__" or "--"
- DO NOT use IDs for styling
- Avoid deep nesting (max 2 levels)

Examples:
  ✅ login-page
  ✅ login-page-background
  ✅ login-card
  ✅ login-form-input

  ❌ login-page__background
  ❌ login-card__title
  ❌ #loginContainer

==================================================
WHEN GENERATING NEW CODE
==================================================
- Follow the folder structure strictly.
- Never invent new architectural patterns.
- Never mix backend and frontend logic.
- Do not introduce external UI libraries unless explicitly asked.
- Prefer clarity over cleverness.
